### Item 1 · the staff Quotes table overflows the page (B347-1)
**Finding (RELAYED `B347_STATUS.md:162`, verbatim):** "**B347-1 · Minor · Quotes list with the staff columns overflows the page at 1440 px.** `web/src/screens/QuoteList.tsx:98-135` + `QuoteList.columns.tsx` (13 columns), the table has no overflow container and the stack-table breakpoint is 390 px. Instrument: Chrome 1440x900, analyst, real API (path B) and stub (406 px). FAIL met: `document.scrollingElement.scrollWidth - innerWidth` = 366 (brief's own check is 0); the Last updated and Action columns fall outside the panel (`pathB-quotes-analyst-1440.png`). Plain personas: 0. Fix-shape: let the table scroll inside its panel (an overflow-x wrapper) or collapse to the card layout below a wider breakpoint when `staff` is on, or tighten the four staff columns; CSS belongs to B310's `styles.css` or a file of the builder's own. Regression: a Playwright check at 1440 px as the analyst asserting page overflow 0 and the Action button lies inside the panel box (red today)."
**Facts on `main` (MEASURED 23:3x by `gh api` reads of the sha above):** `QueueTable` is defined in `QuoteList.tsx` (`:89`, `<table className="stack-table">`) and is used by the Quotes list at `:243` inside `<section className="panel" aria-label="Quote list">`; the stack-table card layout starts at **600 px** (`styles.css` `@media (max-width: 600px)`, not 390 as the gate wrote: say which you measure). `styles.css:74` already has `.table-wrap { overflow-x: auto; position: relative; }`; `th, td` carry `white-space: nowrap` (`:77`). The persona id for the analyst is `analyst` (`personas.ts`); in stub mode the analyst reads the Quotes list from the stub's synthetic rows (`stubApi.ts` `listQuotes`), so this item needs **no API process**. **Style rules:** brand tokens are the `:root` variables at the top of `styles.css` (`--surface`, `--line`, `--muted`, `--text`, `--brand`, `--accent`, `--th-bg`, `--hover-bg`, …); no style-guide file exists in the repo (MEASURED: tree search for style/brand/design finds only CSS files and `cssColourGuard`). **Invent no colour:** a new rule uses an existing token or none; `cssColourGuard` is the repo's own guard for colour literals; do not add a hex, rgb or named colour.
**Do (R-W20-1, defaults):**
